  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d give every person a deep, instinctive empathy for everyone else\u2014so that before acting, we\u2019d naturally feel and respect others\u2019 joys, fears and needs.  \n \nWhy empathy?  \n\u2022 It underpins cooperation. When we truly understand someone else\u2019s perspective, we\u2019re far more likely to seek win-win solutions than to compete or cling to prejudice.  \n\u2022 It drives generosity. Empathy turns abstract statistics\u2014\u201cmillions in poverty,\u201d \u201crefugees fleeing war\u201d\u2014into real, relatable human lives deserving of help.  \n\u2022 It calms conflict. Many disputes, from personal arguments to international wars, stem from dehumanizing the \u201cother.\u201d Empathy bridges that gulf.  \n\nWith universal empathy, problems like inequality, environmental destruction, and violence would still require action\u2014but people would be far more motivated to work together on lasting, humane solutions. Empathy wouldn\u2019t solve every challenge overnight, but it would transform how we face them: as one interconnected human family rather than competing tribes.",
